abstract: >
  The Ψ-Ontic Reality Model (ΨORM) is a unified framework that repositions
  consciousness as the primary agent of reality navigation. It proposes that
  time is not fundamental, that consciousness navigates static frozen moments
  through frequency synchronization, and that shared reality is an emergent
  property of frequency alignment between consciousness vectors. This work
  includes the complete seed document, falsifiable predictions, glossary, and
  supporting materials.
